From 675bd4e8cf23accbc46281380bd510f2e96c08df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corvid <corvid@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:46:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Corvid v1.7: failover stall times in the panel, RTMP ack fix

- The silence after which a fallback (the backup) is left for the next
  one (the waiting picture) is a setting of its own (FallbackStall,
  default: the primary's Stall). A flaky backup line stays on air through
  short gaps instead of flipping to the waiting picture.
- Both stall times change at run time, also for connected players:
  GET/PUT /api/v3/fork/failover (PUT admin only), stored in
  <db>/failover.json and applied at start over the CORE_RTMP_FAILOVER_*
  defaults.
- joy4 (vendored): the RTMP Acknowledgement carried the bytes since the
  last acknowledgement instead of the sequence number (total bytes
  received, RTMP spec 5.4.3). Clients with flow control could stall.
  Note: keep this change when re-vendoring.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UhjysExATCKDyVfUWLA89B
